{"id":9624,"date":"2025-10-15T05:18:58","date_gmt":"2025-10-15T05:18:58","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/?p=9624"},"modified":"2025-10-15T05:18:58","modified_gmt":"2025-10-15T05:18:58","slug":"uncovering-the-secret-lives-of-ants-rodents-in-melbourne-homes-pest-exterminator-melbourne","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/uncovering-the-secret-lives-of-ants-rodents-in-melbourne-homes-pest-exterminator-melbourne\/","title":{"rendered":"Uncovering the Secret Lives of Ants &#038; Rodents in Melbourne Homes \u2013 Pest Exterminator Melbourne"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ants and rodents are two of the most common yet underestimated household pests in Melbourne.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While you might occasionally see a trail of ants on your kitchen bench or hear faint scratching in your ceiling at night, these subtle signs often indicate a much larger hidden problem.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Melbourne\u2019s changing weather conditions and urban landscape make it an ideal environment for ants and rodents to thrive.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Once they find food, warmth, and shelter, they settle in and multiply quickly. Ignoring early signs of infestation can lead to food contamination, property damage, and even health issues.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This is why hiring a professional pest control service is essential. Experienced exterminators can identify the root cause of infestations, treat them effectively, and prevent them from returning.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/\"><b>7 States Pest Control<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> is one such trusted name in Melbourne, providing reliable and safe pest extermination services for homes and businesses alike.<\/span><\/p>\n<h2><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Understanding Ants in Melbourne Homes<\/span><\/h2>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-9627\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-10-at-12.20.36-PM-300x164.jpeg\" alt=\"pest exterminator melbourne\n\" width=\"300\" height=\"164\" srcset=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-10-at-12.20.36-PM-300x164.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-10-at-12.20.36-PM-1024x559.jpeg 1024w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-10-at-12.20.36-PM-768x419.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-10-at-12.20.36-PM.jpeg 1408w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ants are small but incredibly organised insects. They live in colonies that can grow into thousands and are constantly on the lookout for food and water sources. Once they find a steady supply, they establish trails to transport it back to their nests \u2014 often inside your home.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Common Ant Species in Melbourne<\/b><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Black House Ants:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Commonly seen in kitchens and bathrooms, they are attracted to sugary and greasy food.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Argentine Ants:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Known for forming large colonies and spreading quickly between homes.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Coastal Brown Ants:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Usually nest under pavers, lawns, and along footpaths.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Carpenter Ants:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Unlike other ants, these can damage timber while building their nests inside wood structures.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><b>Habits and Behaviour<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ants are social insects that work together in colonies. They communicate using pheromones, creating scent trails that lead other ants to food sources. These trails are often seen near benches, sinks, or pet food bowls.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"><br \/>\n<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> They prefer nesting in warm, protected areas such as inside walls, under floors, and around foundations. During summer, their activity increases, making infestations more noticeable.<\/span><\/p>\n<h3><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Understanding Rodents in Melbourne Homes<\/span><\/h3>\n<p><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"alignnone size-medium wp-image-9626\" src=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-10-at-12.35.39-PM-300x164.jpeg\" alt=\"pest exterminator melbourne\n\" width=\"300\" height=\"164\" srcset=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-10-at-12.35.39-PM-300x164.jpeg 300w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-10-at-12.35.39-PM-1024x559.jpeg 1024w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-10-at-12.35.39-PM-768x419.jpeg 768w, https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-10-at-12.35.39-PM.jpeg 1408w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 300px) 100vw, 300px\" \/><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While ants are a nuisance, rodents pose a more serious risk to both property and health. Rats and mice are intelligent, adaptable, and capable of squeezing through extremely small gaps to enter your home.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Common Rodents Found in Melbourne<\/b><\/p>\n<ol>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>House Mouse:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Small, fast, and often found in roof voids, cupboards, and behind appliances.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Norway Rat:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Larger in size and prefers basements, garages, or lower floors.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Roof Rat:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Excellent climbers that nest in ceilings, attics, and upper areas of buildings.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ol>\n<p><b>How Rodents Enter and Hide<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Rodents can enter through small cracks, broken vents, or gaps under doors and around pipes. Once inside, they seek out food sources and nesting spots in dark, quiet areas. Kitchens, roof cavities, and storage areas are their preferred hiding places.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Damage and Health Risks<\/b><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Structural Damage<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: Rodents chew through wood, insulation, and electrical wiring, creating fire hazards.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Food Contamination:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Their droppings and urine can contaminate food storage areas.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Health Concerns:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Rodents carry diseases like leptospirosis and salmonella, posing serious risks to humans and pets.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A single rodent sighting often indicates more hiding nearby. Early detection and professional treatment are key to preventing widespread infestation.<\/span><\/p>\n<h4><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Comparing Ants vs Rodents<\/span><\/h4>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Although ants and rodents are both pests, their behaviours and the severity of their impact differ greatly.<\/span><\/p>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Aspect<\/b><\/td>\n<td><b>Ants<\/b><\/td>\n<td><b>Rodents<\/b><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Activity Period<\/b><\/td>\n<td><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Mostly during warmer months<\/span><\/td>\n<td><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Year-round, especially in winter<\/span><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Signs of Infestation<\/b><\/td>\n<td><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Trails, nests, dirt piles<\/span><\/td>\n<td><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Droppings, gnaw marks, scratching sounds<\/span><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Type of Damage<\/b><\/td>\n<td><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Food contamination<\/span><\/td>\n<td><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Structural and electrical damage<\/span><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Health Risks<\/b><\/td>\n<td><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Low to moderate<\/span><\/td>\n<td><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">High<\/span><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Treatment Urgency<\/b><\/td>\n<td><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Moderate<\/span><\/td>\n<td><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Urgent<\/span><\/td>\n<\/tr>\n<\/tbody>\n<\/table>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While ants can create hygiene issues, rodents demand immediate attention due to their destructive nature and disease risk.<\/span><\/p>\n<h5><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">How a Professional Pest Exterminator in Melbourne Can Help<\/span><\/h5>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Professional exterminators have the knowledge, tools, and experience to address infestations safely and effectively.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Inspection and Identification<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The first step is a thorough inspection. Pest experts identify the type of pest, nesting areas, and entry points. Understanding the source of the problem ensures that treatment is both targeted and efficient.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Effective Treatment Options<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Professionals use safe and environmentally friendly treatments designed to eliminate pests without harming your household. Common methods include:<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Ant Baiting Systems:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> These target entire colonies by attracting worker ants, which carry the bait back to the nest.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Rodent Control Stations:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Secure bait stations and traps eliminate rodents while preventing accidental exposure to pets or children.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Entry Point Sealing:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Blocking cracks, vents, and gaps helps prevent re-entry.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><b>Long-Term Prevention<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pest exterminators also focus on prevention. They provide practical advice on maintaining cleanliness, managing waste, and sealing potential entry points. Follow-up visits ensure pests do not return.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Choosing an experienced pest exterminator in Melbourne, such as <\/span><b>7 States Pest Control<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, ensures that infestations are handled thoroughly and safely.<\/span><\/p>\n<h6><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">DIY vs Professional Pest Control<\/span><\/h6>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">It\u2019s tempting to try DIY methods, especially when the problem seems small. However, these home remedies often provide only short-term results.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Common DIY Methods<\/b><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Using sprays, powders, or traps from hardware stores.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cleaning surfaces with vinegar or bleach.<\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Placing bait or homemade deterrents like peppermint oil or cloves.<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While these may reduce visible pests temporarily, they rarely eliminate colonies or hidden nests.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Advantages of Hiring a Professional<\/b><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Accurate Identification<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">: Professionals can distinguish between pest species and apply the right treatment.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\n<p><\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Safe and Effective Products:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Licensed exterminators use products not available to the public, ensuring better and safer results.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\n<p><\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Time and Cost Efficiency:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> A professional service eliminates the problem at its source, saving you time and repeated expenses.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\n<p><\/span><\/li>\n<li style=\"font-weight: 400;\" aria-level=\"1\"><b>Guaranteed Results:<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> Most pest control companies offer service guarantees and follow-up inspections.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\n<p><\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Investing in professional pest control is a long-term solution that ensures your home remains pest-free.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ants and rodents are persistent invaders in Melbourne homes, often hiding where you least expect them. Ignoring early warning signs can lead to costly repairs, food contamination, and health hazards.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Prompt action through professional pest control not only removes the visible pests but also tackles the root of the infestation. Whether it\u2019s a trail of ants in the kitchen or the sound of scratching in your ceiling, it\u2019s best not to wait until the problem worsens.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For safe, effective, and professional <\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/\"><b>pest extermination in Melbourne,<\/b><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> contact <\/span><b>7 States Pest Control<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">. Their experienced team provides comprehensive inspection, treatment, and prevention services to keep your home protected all year round.<\/span><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Ants and rodents are two of the most common yet underestimated household pests in Melbourne.\u00a0 While you might occasionally see a trail of ants on your kitchen bench or hear faint scratching in your ceiling at night, these subtle signs often indicate a much larger hidden problem. Melbourne\u2019s changing weather conditions and urban landscape make [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":9625,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"footnotes":""},"categories":[21],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-9624","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-rodent-pest-control"],"yoast_head":"<!-- This site is optimized with the Yoast SEO plugin v25.4 - https:\/\/yoast.com\/wordpress\/plugins\/seo\/ -->\n<title>Ant &amp; Rodent Control | Pest Exterminator Melbourne<\/title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Protect your home from ants and rodents. Get expert pest extermination from trusted Melbourne professionals for safe and lasting results\" \/>\n<meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow, max-snippet:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-video-preview:-1\" \/>\n<link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/uncovering-the-secret-lives-of-ants-rodents-in-melbourne-homes-pest-exterminator-melbourne\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_US\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"article\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"Ant &amp; Rodent Control | Pest Exterminator Melbourne\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"Protect your home from ants and rodents. Get expert pest extermination from trusted Melbourne professionals for safe and lasting results\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/uncovering-the-secret-lives-of-ants-rodents-in-melbourne-homes-pest-exterminator-melbourne\/\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n<meta property=\"article:published_time\" content=\"2025-10-15T05:18:58+00:00\" \/>\n<meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/10\/WhatsApp-Image-2025-10-14-at-4.06.48-PM.jpeg\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1280\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"672\" \/>\n\t<meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image\/jpeg\" \/>\n<meta name=\"author\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" \/>\n<meta name=\"twitter:label1\" content=\"Written by\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data1\" content=\"7 States Pest Control\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:label2\" content=\"Est. reading time\" \/>\n\t<meta name=\"twitter:data2\" content=\"6 minutes\" \/>\n<script type=\"application\/ld+json\" class=\"yoast-schema-graph\">{\"@context\":\"https:\/\/schema.org\",\"@graph\":[{\"@type\":\"Article\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/uncovering-the-secret-lives-of-ants-rodents-in-melbourne-homes-pest-exterminator-melbourne\/#article\",\"isPartOf\":{\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/uncovering-the-secret-lives-of-ants-rodents-in-melbourne-homes-pest-exterminator-melbourne\/\"},\"author\":{\"name\":\"7 States Pest Control\",\"@id\":\"https:\/\/7statespestcontrol.com.au\/#\/schema\/person\/d2eebd8e6e8b6f07170a10bc11d3da